4. Choosing a framework

I would pick CrewAI for this project because the work is a fixed assembly line: research, then write, then edit. CrewAI’s agent/task/crew vocabulary maps directly onto that, and Process.sequential handles passing output between steps with almost no code. Changing the writer’s behavior took a few lines in one Agent definition.

The Agents SDK kit from class works differently. Its Triage agent hands off to specialists (Math Tutor, Writing Coach, Translator), and the model decides who gets the request. That would be easier for a routing problem, such as one chat interface for many request types. It would be harder here, because I want every request to pass through all three roles in order, and hand-offs leave that to the model.

LangGraph would be easier if I wanted a loop or a tool. The graph in class (agent, tools, and an edge back to the agent) made tool use visible, and conditional edges would let me send a draft back to the writer when the editor flags too many unsupported claims. My crew has no tools, so I can’t check a single fact it states. It would also be harder for the simple linear case, since I would have to define nodes, edges, and state myself.

